<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>User Interface Design on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/categories/user-interface-design/</link><description>Recent content in User Interface Design on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:09:22 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/categories/user-interface-design/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Google debuts 'Create My Widget' AI tool for custom home screen widgets on Pixel devices</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/google-debuts-create-my-widget-ai-tool-for-custom-home-screen-widgets-on-pixel-devices/</link><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:09:22 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/google-debuts-create-my-widget-ai-tool-for-custom-home-screen-widgets-on-pixel-devices/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/DSC04405_processed.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C10.723165084465%2C100%2C78.55366983107&amp;w=1200" alt="Featured image of post Google debuts 'Create My Widget' AI tool for custom home screen widgets on Pixel devices" /&gt;&lt;h1 id="google-debuts-create-my-widget-ai-tool-for-custom-home-screen-widgets-on-pixel-devices"&gt;Google debuts &amp;lsquo;Create My Widget&amp;rsquo; AI tool for custom home screen widgets on Pixel devices
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Google has introduced Create My Widget, an AI-powered feature that lets Pixel users design custom home screen widgets through natural language prompts. The tool, part of Android&amp;rsquo;s Gemini Intelligence suite, is currently in beta and rolling out to Pixel phones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-what-can-you-build"&gt;📱 What Can You Build?
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Create My Widget enables users to generate a variety of functional widgets including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weather-based messages (e.g., &amp;ldquo;Tut tut, looks like rain&amp;rdquo; when precipitation is detected)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entertainment displays (like hourly Jurassic Park quotes from the original film)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal habit trackers (such as logging daily mental health walks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event countdowns (counting down to holidays or calendar events)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sports updates (showing recent scores and upcoming game times)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recipe suggestions (daily three-ingredient cocktail ideas)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-how-it-works"&gt;⚙️ How It Works
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The feature operates as a prompt shortcut for Gemini. When you tap a created widget, it opens the Gemini interface on your home screen, processes your request, and generates the desired output. Some examples:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Widget Type&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Functionality&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Quote Widget&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Displays a different Jurassic Park quote each hour&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Weather Widget&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Shows &amp;ldquo;Tut tut, looks like rain&amp;rdquo; during precipitation, &amp;ldquo;No rain right now&amp;rdquo; otherwise&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Walk Logger&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Triggers Gemini to add a walk to calendar and provides a checklist for marking completed walks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bus Schedule&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Searches for arrival times at a specified stop (though results vary in usefulness)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-availability-and-limitations"&gt;🚀 Availability and Limitations
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently in beta testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rolling out to Pixel phones (tested on Pixel 11 Pro)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creation time: approximately 20 seconds per widget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not a one-size-fits-all solution—some use cases like real-time transit data produce less useful outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Screenshot_20261124-094903.png?quality=90&amp;amp;strip=all&amp;amp;w=2400"
loading="lazy"
alt="figure"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Screenshot_20261124-100716.png?quality=90&amp;amp;strip=all&amp;amp;w=2400"
loading="lazy"
alt="figure"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
